{"name":"Soft Focus","hex":"#e2efdd","fetched":"2026-10-13","looked":{"definitions":[{"term":"soft focus","whole":true,"parts":[{"part":"Noun","definitions":["The blur produced by spherical aberration in a lens, sometimes deliberately used to produce a dreamy effect or to eliminate blemishes."]}],"link":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/soft_focus"}],"entries":[{"title":"Soft Focus (Euroboys album)","blocks":[{"text":"Soft Focus is the fifth album released by the Norwegian band Euroboys. It peaked at #2 on the Norwegian album charts."}],"image":"https://upload.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/en/4/4a/Euroboys_-_Soft_Focus.jpeg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=api&utm_content=thumbnail_unscaled","link":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Soft_Focus_(Euroboys_album)"},{"title":"Soft Focus (Hotel Fiction album)","blocks":[{"text":"Soft Focus is the first full-length album released by Hotel Fiction, released on August 27, 2021."}],"image":"https://upload.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/en/f/f8/Hotel_Fiction_-_Soft_Focus.jpeg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=api&utm_content=thumbnail_unscaled","link":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Soft_Focus_(Hotel_Fiction_album)"},{"title":"Soft focus","blocks":[{"text":"In photography, soft focus occurs when a camera lens forms images that are blurred\ndue to uncorrected spherical aberration. A soft focus lens deliberately introduces spherical aberration which blurs fine texture in the image while retaining sharp edges across areas of high contrast; it is not the same as an out-of-focus image, and the effect cannot be achieved simply by defocusing a sharp lens. Soft focus is also the name of the style of photograph produced by such a lens."}],"image":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/e/ee/Bottle_Softfocus_2.jpg/330px-Bottle_Softfocus_2.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=api&utm_content=thumbnail","link":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Soft_focus"}],"images":[{"srcset":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/t